meson: take the MoltenVK/Vulkan include directory from an option, not from Homebrew

Applies to: slp/virglrenderer tag 0.10.4e-krunkit (bfec2d27c3953ee0530c459c2f5d042c2b619fa1).

With -Dvenus=true the fork's meson.build adds
-I/opt/homebrew/opt/molten-vk/libexec/include to every C compile. The Venus
headers (src/venus/venus-protocol/vulkan_core.h) include "vk_video/*.h", which
the fork does not ship, and that directory is where the author's Homebrew
"molten-vk" formula keeps them. So the build only works on a machine with that
exact Homebrew layout, and on a machine that has the formula installed it picks
up whatever version of the headers Homebrew has. The Venus spike worked around
this with CFLAGS, which leaves the Homebrew path in the compile line.

Add a string option, moltenvk-include-dir (default empty = add nothing), and use
it instead of the hard-coded path. build-libs.sh passes the include directory
that belongs to the MoltenVK it just built (Package/Release/MoltenVK/include,
which has vulkan/ and vk_video/). The build no longer depends on, or looks at,
/opt/homebrew.

Upstream status: not applicable (macOS-fork-only build logic).

---
 meson.build       | 5 ++++-
 meson_options.txt | 7 +++++++
 2 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
index ba4692b..3b2d7aa 100644
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -278,7 +278,10 @@ if with_venus
    endif

    add_project_link_arguments('-lMoltenVK', language : 'c')
-   add_project_arguments('-I/opt/homebrew/opt/molten-vk/libexec/include', language : 'c')
+   moltenvk_include_dir = get_option('moltenvk-include-dir')
+   if moltenvk_include_dir != ''
+      add_project_arguments('-I' + moltenvk_include_dir, language : 'c')
+   endif

    conf_data.set('ENABLE_VENUS', 1)

diff --git a/meson_options.txt b/meson_options.txt
index c64cbed..8c72f66 100644
--- a/meson_options.txt
+++ b/meson_options.txt
@@ -52,6 +52,13 @@ option(
   description : 'enable the validation layer for venus'
 )

+option(
+  'moltenvk-include-dir',
+  type : 'string',
+  value : '',
+  description : 'macOS, with venus: folder with the Vulkan headers that go with MoltenVK (vulkan/, vk_video/)'
+)
+
 option(
   'check-gl-errors',
   type : 'boolean',
